WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:06.899
Music playing

00:00:06.899 --> 00:00:10.960
If you're planning on vacation in
Florida this weekend

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.760
looks like you're going to have a
beautiful weather with clear sunny days

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.510
about 70 degrees.

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:22.239
Music playing

00:00:22.239 --> 00:00:25.500
Music playing

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.020
Music playing

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:30.580
Ever wonder why the weatherman is
sometimes just

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:34.740
wrong? Why can't the weatherman predict
more than a few days at a time?

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:38.670
Your local weatherman works with a
team of meteorologists

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:41.820
to create the weather predictions that you see on TV.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:45.120
The beauty of whether is that it is
ever-changing.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.270
This complexity only allows
meteorologist the ability to create

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:53.700
educated forecast based on past and
present weather conditions, rather than

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.140
perfect predictions.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:58.800
Meteorologist use thermometers, to
measure temperature,

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.270
barometers, for air pressure, and
anemometers, for Wind speed.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:06.990
They send weather balloons carrying
these instruments into the atmosphere

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:11.360
to collect data about current weather
conditions. This information,

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:14.950
along with information about cloud
patterns, precipitation,

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:18.590
and other measurements collected by
satellite and radar, is then

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:21.720
plugged into forecasting models in
super computers.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.890
The forecasting models use equations

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:29.030
to create a computerized representation
of the atmosphere.

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:33.039
Previous weather trends and
knowledge of the right equations help to

00:01:33.039 --> 00:01:34.679
predict future patterns, though

00:01:34.679 --> 00:01:38.190
only for a short period. The farther into
the future,

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:41.720
the greater chance of error in the
prediction, which explains why the

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:42.759
weather man can only

00:01:42.759 --> 00:01:47.610
give predictions for around a week at a time. For a family planning a trip a few months

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:48.679
ahead,

00:01:48.679 --> 00:01:52.119
it might be better to rely on the
overall climate of the destination

00:01:52.119 --> 00:01:55.920
rather than the daily weather. A weatherman's predictions

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:00.360
span a few days or a week, while a
climatologists predictions

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:03.070
span years to centuries.

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:06.510
A climatologist doesn't forecast the
weather far in advance,

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:10.560
but rather projects it. This is less percise,

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.980
but it will give you a general idea of what
the range of possible forecasts could be.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:19.950
climatologist help society plan its
activities far in advance,

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:23.570
designed its buildings and
infrastructure, and anticipate the

00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:25.430
effects of different climate conditions.

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:28.860
Climatologist work with architects and
engineers

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:32.250
to recommend strategies to manage
uncomfortable humidity,

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:35.320
heavy rainfall and extreme temperatures

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:39.280
as well as storms, melting polar ice,
monsoons

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:44.480
and sea level. Climatology uses
meteorological data gathered over many

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:45.230
years,

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:49.680
such as records have rainfall,
temperature atmospheric composition,

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:53.760
and synthesizes the data using
statistical and mathematical models.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.810
These models are much like weather
models, but take into account

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:01.130
factors that affect the likelihood of
weather patterns decades

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:05.350
or centuries in advance. So, next time
you're planning a vacation,

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:08.980
make sure you research the climate in
advance and check the weather right

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:09.970
before we leave.

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:14.230
Researching climate can tell you that
you won't need short in Alaska

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:17.400
and it's sunny twice as often as it's
rainy in Rhode Island.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:20.900
However. the weather report might tell
you to bring a raincoat to Rhode Island

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:21.459
anyway,

00:03:21.459 --> 00:03:25.070
depending on that week's forecast. Keep
in mind

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:28.300
that weather is subject to change whereas climate

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:32.360
will give you a general idea of what to
expect. Happy Travels!

